    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\n\r\nMaybe it is related to this second issue listed in the help file:\r\n\r\n> Known issues which won't be resolved:\r\n> - ...\r\n> - During search for builtin textobjects there is no distinction if it is\r\n  inside string or comment. For example, in the following case there will\r\n  be wrong match for a function call: `f(a = \")\", b = 1)`.\r\n\r\nbut the inner tag yank is not correct when a tag has an attribute whose value contains a `>` character.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFor example with this tag (`^` is cursor position):\r\n\r\n```\r\n<a onclick={() => { /* ... */ }}>link</a>\r\n                                   ^\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`vit` should select this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<a onclick={() => { /* ... */ }}>link</a>\r\n                                 ----\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nActually, it selects this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<a onclick={() => { /* ... */ }}>link</a>\r\n                 --------------------\r\n```",
