            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for creating an issue!\r\n\r\nYes, unfortunately, this is a limitation of a Lua pattern based approach: I don't see a way of how to distinct which of the `>` is actually a closing an opening tag. Did you look into using treesitter here? Maybe it might help.",
