            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "It works using TreeSitter. Actually, I defined a mapping directly in the settings of the `nvim-treesitter.textobjects` plugin:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntextObjects = {\r\n    select = {\r\n        keymaps = {\r\n            ['at'] = '@function.outer',\r\n            ['it'] = '@function.inner',\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor the `html` filetype, `@function.outer` allows to select a tag, and `@function.inner` allows to select an inner tag.",
            "created_at": "2022-08-11T17:22:34Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212271855",
