        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It works using TreeSitter.\r\n\r\nThat is great!\r\n\r\nIt sure should work when mapping is defined in 'nvim-treesitter.textobjects', but with following caveats:\r\n- If you type `a`, then wait for some time (`timeoutlen` milliseconds), and then type `t`, it will use 'mini.ai' textobject. This is due to how 'mini.ai' creates mappings and Neovim resolves them.\r\n- You won't benefit from 'mini.ai' search method, consecutive application, and 'next'/'last' textobjects.\r\n\r\nI would suggest creating 'after/ftplugin/html.lua' file and define `vim.b.miniai_config` buffer local variable there like so:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal spec_treesitter = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter\r\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    t = spec_treesitter({ a = '@function.outer', i = '@function.inner' }),\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2022-08-11T17:29:22Z",
